## System Architecture Blueprint: Zero-Latency Dual-Texture Object Tracking
This document serves as the final engineering alignment blueprint for developers and AI agents onboarding onto this project. It synthesizes the full scope of our design iterations, physical manufacturing requirements, software optimization loops, and final deployment strategies.
------------------------------
## 1. System Overview & The Core Breakthrough
The objective of this project is to implement an ultra-low-overhead, zero-latency 3D object detection and tracking system that runs alongside other resource-heavy computer vision tasks without bottlenecking the main host processor.
Instead of deploying a computationally heavy AI model (like a deep-learning object detector), this architecture splits the tracking problem into two highly optimized, complementary streams:

   1. The Physical Layer (Visual Contrast via Texture): A single-color, 100% stealth-black hardware casing embedded with a dual-texture geometric marker (e.g., an ArUco grid or a continuous infinity loop logo).
   2. The Hardware Telemetry Layer (Orientation): An onboard Inertial Measurement Unit (IMU) mounted directly to the physical box, broadcasting real-time 3D rotation metrics wirelessly to the camera host device.

------------------------------
## 2. Physical & Manufacturing Specifications
To maintain absolute human visual stealth while providing an explicit, high-contrast digital signature for standard RGB cameras, the hardware casing must be manufactured using the following stepped, multi-texture profile:

      [Outer Edge of Pitch-Black Casing]
__________________              __________________  <- Protects against impact/scratches

                  |            |
                  | [Matte BG] |  <- Mold-Tech MT-11020 Coarse Texture (Traps Light)
                  |____    ____|
                       |  |
                       |__|       <- SPI A-1 Mirror-Polished Gloss Block (Bounces Light)
                       
                [Recessed Pocket]


* The Recessed Pocket: The entire target tracking pad must be sunken into a 1.0mm to 1.5mm deep protective pocket on the device casing. When the device impacts surfaces or slides across the ground, the outer edge takes 100% of the friction, keeping the internal data features scratch-proof.
* The Background (Matte Floor): Specified as a heavy bead-blast texture finish, such as [Mold-Tech MT-11020](https://www.google.com/search?kgmid=FAILED_OR_SKIPPED) or [MT-11030](https://www.google.com/search?kgmid=FAILED_OR_SKIPPED). This creates an ultra-rough surface that scatters and traps light, appearing dead matte-black to the camera from any angle.
* The Target Shapes (Gloss Blocks): Raised 0.5mm from the matte floor (but kept safely below the outer case rim). These shapes are specified with a diamond-buff mirror polish finish, such as [SPI A-1](https://www.google.com/search?kgmid=FAILED_OR_SKIPPED) or [SPI A-2](https://www.google.com/search?kgmid=FAILED_OR_SKIPPED). They act as pure mirrors, bouncing a bright burst of light (specular reflection) directly back into the camera lens.

